# CodeLink SOLUTION design system

Every UI change must follow this look. Do not revert to a generic flat SaaS header or palette.

## Brand tokens only

Use `src/theme/colors.ts` (`brand`, `colors`, `royalAlpha`, `cyanAlpha`). Never introduce new hues.

- Cyan `#00AEFE` — reserved accents: CTAs, active fills, hairlines
- Royal `#1D68BE` — reserved for primary buttons and open/hover fills
- Charcoal `#54595E` / near-black `#111111` — default titles, nav labels, body
- White `#FFFFFF` — light surfaces
- Dark surfaces — `#0B1220` page, `#162033` cards (never invent extra hues)

Do **not** paint brand blue on every heading or menu title. Default type stays charcoal/black in light, off-white in dark. Brand color appears only where it earns attention (CTA, active state, hover fill).

Light/dark is class-based (`html.dark`). Use `var(--background)`, `var(--text-primary)`, and `ThemeToggle`. Persist with `codelink-theme`. Header uses `logos.header` in light and `logos.footer` in dark.

## Visual language

- Glossy, unique motion — not a generic flat SaaS look
- Top nav: thick gradient fill on hover/open. Dropdown rows stay calmer
- Mega-menus: Codevian columns; AWS-style Products rail + grid
- Solid white dropdowns (no see-through homepage)
- Motion is smooth (`0.35–0.5s`, ease-out)

## Visual language

- Glossy glass: frosted white, soft royal glow, cyan→royal hairlines
- Unique, not stock: liquid color-fill hovers, sheen sweeps, staggered motion
- Mega-menus stay structured (Codevian columns; AWS-style Products rail + grid)
- Motion is smooth (`0.35–0.5s`, ease-out). No abrupt pops

## Header contract

- Logo: `logos.header` in nav, `logos.footer` in footer
- Nav: Services, Technology Focus, Products, Career, Company, Work, Blog, Contact us
- Products panel: left category rail, right content grid, close control

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — generic flat link
<a className="text-gray-600 hover:text-blue-600">Services</a>

// ✅ GOOD — brand fill + cyan underline
<button className="nav-link-premium">Services</button>
```
